    A group of rows: contiguous rows on a container with large corners, as the
    system Settings app has used for several versions. androidx.preference does
    not provide it.

    Measured from a Pixel 8's Settings at 365 dpi, since there is no published
    spec: the radii by fitting a circle to the corner's alpha profile, the rest
    by finding the container's edges in a screenshot. The results were 15.8 dp
    and 14.9 dp for the two ends of a group, 3.95 dp between rows, 2.19 dp of
    gap, 20.6 dp between groups and 15.78 dp either side.
-->
<resources>

    <dimen name="group_radius">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_radius_inner">4dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_inset">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_gap">2dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="group_spacing">20dp</dimen>
    <!-- Either side of a row that is its own container: a text field's box
         has no card behind it, and a 2 dp gap next to one looks like an error. -->
    <dimen name="group_gap_field">8dp</dimen>

    <!-- Around a card on the home screen. With the list's own padding this
         adds up to the 16 dp inset of a group of rows. -->
    <dimen name="card_margin">8dp</dimen>

    <!--
        A screen's header is a heading over the groups below it and is inset
        like one: 24 dp, where a container's edge is at 16. Flush with the
        container looks unaligned, because the 16 dp corner puts the content
        inside it further in than the edge.

        A header button matches the system's: a 40 dp filled circle centred in
        a 48 dp touch target. The button inset is 4 dp less so that the circle,
        not the touch target, lines up.
    -->
    <dimen name="header_inset">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="header_inset_button">20dp</dimen>

    <!-- Above and below the header. A header is a bar's height wherever it
         appears (as a screen's bar, or over a sheet), so this is what is left
         either side of a 48 dp button. -->
    <dimen name="header_padding">4dp</dimen>

    <!-- Inside a row, and inside a heading over a group of them. -->
    <dimen name="row_padding">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="row_min_height">56dp</dimen>
    <!-- The most of a row an option's name takes before it wraps. Wide enough for
         the longest single word at the body size, so a wrap falls between words. -->
    <dimen name="row_name_max_width">140dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_inset">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_padding_top">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="heading_padding_bottom">12dp</dimen>

</resources>
